ref 17592186668058} {:answer/id #uuid "faca8fbb-502f-56d2-a54e-2182561d9645" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668059}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "faca8fbb-502f-56d2-a54e-2182561d9645" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668059} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f9b9068-c971-55e3-969f-0cdeb2e774d1" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668306}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ff6510c0-b13d-5580-9ffe-72088a4d30a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-38548" :question/problem "![](images/89/89299bca567844fbc51f0bc245acea2b62e6c0de387e18b6052a6608605c0b48.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true in relation to the function $y=f(x)$ above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement “The function is left-continuous at $x=-1$” is false. The function is not left-continuous at $x=-1,$ since the left-sided limit is not equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}f(x)=1\\ne 2=f(-1)\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function is right-continuous at $x=-1$” is false. The function is not right-continuous at $x=-1,$ since the right-sided limit is not equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{+}}f(x)=3\\ne 2=f(-1)\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function is continuous at $x=-1$” is false. In order for the function to be continuous at $x=-1,$ it must be both left-continuous and right-continuous. However, we have already determined that the function is neither left-continuous nor right-continuous at this point.\n\nIn conclusion, none of the statements are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078991 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078487 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f00fd821-a5d4-5844-9db5-795b9e321b94" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Largest Intervals of Continuity of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7332aef-d1ab-59ae-b512-ef545f7ae744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460053} {:answer/id #uuid "a7b71dc6-74e7-5711-981c-28e960d8262e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460054}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7332aef-d1ab-59ae-b512-ef545f7ae744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460053} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7e35449-b18a-5d0d-86fa-ec4cdb318007" :answer-field/key "$x\\in (-\\infty ,0]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460893} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f03cdec-2456-5c07-b8c8-14bc004724e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460055} {:answer/id #uuid "88b46501-e9aa-54d5-93ba-48e2c0121e50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460056}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88b46501-e9aa-54d5-93ba-48e2c0121e50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460056} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea9228a9-88cb-5187-97b8-045712012a79" :answer-field/key "$x\\in [-3,2]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460894} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c83dd0f1-8727-5449-875d-e38cccc8260e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460057} {:answer/id #uuid "c43d342a-d212-5d50-8724-f2ad92cd2387" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460058}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c83dd0f1-8727-5449-875d-e38cccc8260e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460057} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3bda150-9207-5a54-ae72-a77156a194f2" :answer-field/key "$x\\in (0,\\infty )$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460895} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bdf2a8d-7930-5bb6-a44b-d34cb6fd5f5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668090} {:answer/id #uuid "6ca87491-9735-5503-bb3f-9a286176a1ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668091}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0bdf2a8d-7930-5bb6-a44b-d34cb6fd5f5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668090} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5bbb80a-da2a-5ed2-b13c-0a291f1b081e" :answer-field/key "The function is not continuous on any of the given intervals" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "183472b0-16c2-5809-99fd-33beade724a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-48344" :question/problem "![](images/09/09d006953b4fc1d111a84e78fcc6b2038d53768fb82d6f61a0b2a1d0126bbb40.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ above. On which of the following intervals is the function continuous? \n\nYou may assume that all points of discontinuity of $f(x)$ are shown in the diagram.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement.\n\n- The function is *not* continuous on $(-\\infty ,0]$ because it contains a discontinuity at $x=-3.$\n\n- The function is continuous on $[-3,2].$ It is continuous on $(-3,2),$ and also right continuous at $x=-3$ and left continuous at $x=2.$\n\n- The function is *not* continuous on $(0,\\infty )$ because it contains a discontinuity at $x=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x\\in [-3,2]$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078992 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078487 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f00fd821-a5d4-5844-9db5-795b9e321b94" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Largest Intervals of Continuity of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1abb4819-32aa-5825-8aba-4fd7804637a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460059} {:answer/id #uuid "f35e1f11-2422-51e5-af6e-1235b12fd7b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460060}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1abb4819-32aa-5825-8aba-4fd7804637a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460059} :answer-field/id #uuid "43e016e3-9a6a-572e-859b-c5130dd62a24" :answer-field/key "$x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460896} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1283eade-08fd-5f30-9ef4-1519d117e848" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460061} {:answer/id #uuid "c48d2474-80c0-579a-8b13-6c238bde32de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460062}] :answer-field/co