e "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668122} {:answer/id #uuid "1b6d0ed3-3b42-55e2-bc73-9ad62fa01bb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668123}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3032a8c2-0156-5be3-9219-d5b32f36ed21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668122} :answer-field/id #uuid "f405d2fc-0902-5b27-8186-1ca98ea779e0" :answer-field/key "The function has no vertical asymptotes" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668338}] :question/id #uuid "38d33573-721b-5c42-99c6-39f5804f5848" :question/math-academy-id "q-80690" :question/problem "Calculate the vertical asymptotes of $f(x) = (x)/(x(x - 2))$.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "After cancellation, $f(x)=\\frac{1}{x - 2}$. Its real denominator zeros are $\\left\\{2\\right\\}$; canceled factors produce holes, not vertical asymptotes."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088417 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c04b23-e341-57e9-a072-985e4b536e5a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linear Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed20dcfb-93aa-5edf-8467-1766b4b4b822" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477473} {:answer/id #uuid "d32af6f8-8b0f-5234-806c-62e9d747df5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477474}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d32af6f8-8b0f-5234-806c-62e9d747df5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477474} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c20384a-0816-5afd-a2d2-3cd169248491" :answer-field/key "$T(kv)=kT(v)$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vector $v$ and real scalar $k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477706} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93078b9b-9d6c-5f09-8800-51a8a1ec8bbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477475} {:answer/id #uuid "2ea56d0c-ed1c-5b1a-8bbd-91e911ada20d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477476}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ea56d0c-ed1c-5b1a-8bbd-91e911ada20d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477476} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdecd740-b0ed-58be-95a9-c0e256d73db9" :answer-field/key "$T({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2})$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477707} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4df3c9b-0f75-5bb2-b7f3-076984d785f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477477} {:answer/id #uuid "f15219cd-4112-5f94-bd53-1aa374fbf965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f15219cd-4112-5f94-bd53-1aa374fbf965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477478} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c819544-8a99-529a-8823-7309e6fe05a9" :answer-field/key "$T$ is a linear transformation" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477708} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6f7adb9-b03b-5ccf-b4b6-058a03c8a4e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668132} {:answer/id #uuid "cef7642b-6f96-5f33-9ceb-d096444d43c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668133}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6f7adb9-b03b-5ccf-b4b6-058a03c8a4e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668132} :answer-field/id #uuid "65888345-1605-5140-8d16-6607988f0921" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668343}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a9a96319-3bb3-5dd4-a3ac-27f5effab07d" :question/math-academy-id "q-8331" :question/problem "Let \n$T:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}y \\\\ x\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A linear transformation $T$ satisfies two properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & T\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix}=kT\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\  & T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the first condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}ky \\\\ kx\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =k\\begin{bmatrix}y \\\\ x\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =kT\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the second condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{T}$ is a linear transformation.\n\nAs a result, all three statements are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092602 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092339 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd399539-33cf-5738-b970-fcc6c1d919c8" :knowledge-point/title "Using Properties of Indicator Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d280c1f-3e76-55d8-ac14-ba38ed573031" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459641} {:answer/id #uuid "e59ee5d2-6a44-57d6-8fca-2ab4dfa82d0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459642}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d280c1f-3e76-55d8-ac14-ba38ed573031" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459641} :answer-field/id #uuid "6bd85771-4fdf-5781-aec0-77a096dcc550" :answer-field/key "${1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(5)=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460687} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "932e5b72-2412-5425-a69f-1c5c9b00d4cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459643} {:answer/id #uuid "ff2bf056-35d3-5548-b9d8-14d1a0e85708" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459644}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff2bf056-35d3-5548-b9d8-14d1a0e85708" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459644} :answer-field/id #uuid "003c01a6-9fc8-5470-b192-529dcc80605f" :answer-field/key "${1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(5)=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460688} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "139e8020-5633-5b5f-aa89-637381683bba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459645} {:answer/id #uuid "c9da6006-39ab-5503-a7b6-1bedab9fe445" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459646}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "139e8020-5633-5b5f-aa89-637381683bba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459645} :answer-field/id #uuid "10569c31-698f-5e42-8b38-fb51c01be650" :answer-field/key "$5\\in A\\cap B$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460689} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13645072-43f8-5b1a-a593-c4bbe6872a88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667978} {:answer/id #uuid "ef351941-03e8-5292-b46a-6284349c311c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667979}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13645072-43f8-5b1a-a593-c4bbe6872a88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667978} :answer-field/id #uuid "184fb33e-46b3-52b2-abbc-ea6e7899de6a" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668266}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dbfb19de-ef84-5bc1-a24a-a4632bbb8c2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-172721" :question/problem "$$\n{1}_{A}(5)=1,\\,{1}_{B}(5)=0\n$$\n\nGiven the values of the indicator functions of the sets $A$ and $B,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the indicator functions of $\\overset{―}{A},$ $A\\cap B,$ and $A\\cup B$ have the following properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(x) & =1-{1}_{A}(x) \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(x) & =min\\{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)\\} \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(x) & =max\\{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement ${1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(5)=1$ is false while statement ${1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(5)=0$ is true. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(5) & =min\\{{1}_{A}(5),{1}_{B}(5)\\} \\\\  & =min\\{1,0\\} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement $5\\in A\\cap B$ is false. Since ${1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(5)=0,$ we conclude that $5$ does not belong to $A\\cap B.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(5)=0$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097352 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096740 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d14dbef-9a16-537e-a182-87fd6853e543" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Divergent Sequences"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "307c7cf1-5fd8-539a-baf5-43476b1da200" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460191} {:answer/id #uuid "ed3fcb48-ebc2-5e8e-9078-7e2580db3f5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460192}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "307c7cf1-5fd8-539a-baf5-43476b1da200" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460191} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d23e71b-bbc8-5c5f-97bb-805a4e9c6d29" :answer-field/key "${a}_{n}=\\frac{n-1}{{n}^{3}+1}$ for $n\\ge 1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460962} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0219cde5-ece9-54b0-8ffc-80286a692f29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460193} {:answer/id #uuid "3e370409-0e5a-5645-b7a2-56152ac74d7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460194}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0219cde5-ece9-54b0-8ffc-80286a692f29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460193} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9ee3097-d4bf-50d0-95bf-6225fd4600c1" :answer-field/key "${a}_{n}=\\frac{2}{{n}^{3}}$ for $n\\ge 1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460963} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6136d6ba-9486-55c8-88e7-53fdc6a2739a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460195} {:answer/id #uuid "300f1985-42e9-5c1f-9981-13270d98f964" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460196}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "300f1985-42e9-5c1f-9981-13270d98f964" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460196} :answer-field/id #uuid "f264bd79-c732-55ec-8b29-50df8e1604b3" :answer-field/key "${a}_{n}=\\frac{{n}^{3}+3}{3{n}^{2}-n}$ for $n\\ge 1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460964} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3995f471-7081-5e24-b892-3be083f26d0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668104} {:answer/id #uuid "ebd247d0-c026-5a95-8bcc-8b6e75e784c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668105}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3995f471-7081-5e24-b892-3be083f26d0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668104} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1fc04a1-ab5c-59d3-b9cd-bac1872719ed" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668329}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "42d47711-2fa8-573a-a785-99e3eb0e6a31" :question/math-academy-id "q-74055" :question/problem "Which of the following sequences diverge?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each sequence in turn. We need to calculate the limit of each sequence as $n$ approaches at infinity.\n\n- In sequence “${a}_{n}=\\frac{n-1}{{n}^{3}+1}$ for $n\\ge 1$”, the dominant term in the denominator is ${n}^{3},$ so we divide the numerator and the denominator by ${n}^{3}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n} & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{n-1}{{n}^{3}+1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }⁡\\frac{(\\frac{n}{{n}^{3}}-\\frac{1}{{n}^{3}})}{(\\frac{{n}^{3}}{{n}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{{n}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }⁡\\frac{(\\frac{1}{{n}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{{n}^{3}})}{(1+\\frac{1}{{n}^{3}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{0-0}{1+0} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe limit exists, so the sequence converges.\n\n- In sequence “${a}_{n}=\\frac{2}{{n}^{3}}$ for $n\\ge 1$”, the limit is\n\n$$\n{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n}={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{2}{{n}^{3}}=0.\n$$\n\nThe limit exists, so the sequence converges.\n\n- In sequence “${a}_{n}=\\frac{{n}^{3}+3}{3{n}^{2}-n}$ for $n\\ge 1$”, the dominant term in the denominator is $3{n}^{2},$ so we divide the numerator and the denominator by ${n}^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n} & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{{n}^{3}+3}{3{n}^{2}-n} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{{n}^{3}}{{n}^{2}}+\\frac{3}{{n}^{2}})}{(\\frac{3{n}^{2}}{{n}^{2}}-\\frac{n}{{n}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{(n+\\frac{3}{{n}^{2}})}{(3-\\frac{1}{n})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{n+0}{3-0} \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe limit does not exist, so the sequence diverges.\n\nIn conclusion, sequence “${a}_{n}=\\frac{{n}^{3}+3}{3{n}^{2}-n}$ for $n\\ge 1$” diverges."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097373 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2487fa68-ae0e-5137-baea-4f3fc09c2953" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Quadratic Sequence Is Monotonic"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c240dde-1b14-5375-9cc6-4eff4b05028a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460305} {:answer/id #uuid "fa25a0d9-c29d-58c8-a96f-e6096ddc5ff6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c240dde-1b14-5375-9cc6-4eff4b05028a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460305} :answer-field/id #uuid "ceaabf22-07de-51e1-b4af-2d2da5c2ecaf" :answer-field/key "${a}_{n+1}-{a}_{n}\\le 0$ for all $n\\ge 1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461019} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2643bb69-ea37-5510-b5e5-cbe7815b6940" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460307} {:answer/id #uuid "55d69526-e4b5-5475-99c9-6ae4dd47f02a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460308}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55d69526-e4b5-5475-99c9-6ae4dd47f02a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460308} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1cde8a5-8b50-5aaf-8699-0c6dfba4dfe3" :answer-field/key "${a}_{n}$ is an increasing sequence" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461020} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8db6289a-c1bf-5d2e-81a5-03ec79590183" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460309} {:answer/id #uuid "cb8fe348-2d03-501c-af04-63f23b192ae1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460310}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8db6289a-c1bf-5d2e-81a5-03ec79590183" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460309} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ab868a0-2077-5ab1-81b2-e572f1791439" :answer-field/key "${a}_{n}$ is a decreasing sequence" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461021} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f3245e5-e2c6-5823-a308-3adf7651867a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668126} {:answer/id #uuid "209ef381-3239-58a6-8a7b-9b2284d2e7f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668127}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f3245e5-e2c6-5823-a308-3adf7651867a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668126} :answer-field/id #uuid "be1b71c6-b29f-595b-b386-25a47dee5a3e" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668340}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a3853e50-9001-5dfb-9817-609b2adc1080" :question/math-academy-id "q-81083" :question/problem "Given that  ${a}_{n}={n}^{2}-5$ for $n\\ge 1,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Suppose the sequence ${a}_{n}$ is defined for $n\\ge 1.$ To determine whether ${a}_{n}$ is increasing or decreasing, we can use the following test:\n\n- If a sequence ${a}_{n}$ is *increasing,* then for all $n\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}\\ge {a}_{n}\\,⟹\\,{a}_{n+1}-{a}_{n}\\ge 0.\n$$\n\n- If a sequence ${a}_{n}$ is *decreasing,* then for all $n\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}\\le {a}_{n}\\,⟹\\,{a}_{n+1}-{a}_{n}\\le 0.\n$$\n\n- If neither of these conditions holds, the sequence is *neither increasing nor decreasing*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement.\n\n- Statement “${a}_{n+1}-{a}_{n}\\le 0$ for all $n\\ge 1$” is false. Computing the difference ${a}_{n+1}-{a}_{n},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n+1}-{a}_{n} & =(n+1)^{2}-5-({n}^{2}-5) \\\\  & =(n+1)^{2}-5-{n}^{2}+5 \\\\  & ={n}^{2}+2n+1-{n}^{2} \\\\  & =2n+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is *positive* for $n\\ge 1.$\n\nTo see this concretely, set ${b}_{n}=2n+1.$ Computing the first few terms of ${b}_{n}$ we get\n\n$$\n3,\\,5,\\,7,\\,9,\\,…\\,.\n$$\n\n- Statement “${a}_{n}$ is an increasing sequence” is true, whereas statement “${a}_{n}$ is a decreasing sequence” is false. Since ${a}_{n+1}-{a}_{n}\\ge 0$ for all $n\\ge 1,$ we can conclude that ${a}_{n}$ is an increasing sequence.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${a}_{n}$ is an increasing sequence” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101158 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100959 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "80ed79a9-8e39-5c84-9c87-dec266060afc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Solutions to First-Order Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10dd2375-3309-5242-9f4a-93a4d27c3816" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437992} {:answer/id #uuid "b369a12e-1a9e-53c9-a28e-7de7d2f0dd17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437993}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b369a12e-1a9e-53c9-a28e-7de7d2f0dd17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437993} :answer-field/id #uuid "f260d360-832c-5eaf-a407-8777898370d7" :answer-field/key "$y=-2{e}^{-2x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439025} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b2ec8c3-2e15-5684-9c02-a21fd6230b49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437994} {:answer/id #uuid "44b02a34-b812-5969-824c-b1a36338dbbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437995}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b2ec8c3-2e15-5684-9c02-a21fd6230b49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437994} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8de5f6f-2c45-581c-b864-deb370031b0b" :answer-field/key "$y=-2{e}^{x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439026} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a8b9c15-73b7-50fd-80af-8ff120fa6ba2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437996} {:answer/id #uuid "977a699e-8cdd-54d7-b2cb-49b49d93ef59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437997}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a8b9c15-73b7-50fd-80af-8ff120fa6ba2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437996} :answer-field/id #uuid "f011be38-b8ff-5f20-b55b-d93017ba44c0" :answer-field/key "$y=2{e}^{-x}+1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439027} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed2e962f-0c82-5252-b1c3-52a6cbdc5517" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667964} {:answer/id #uuid "6e62fe59-b153-55ef-be33-20f23f86246e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667965}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed2e962f-0c82-5252-b1c3-52a6cbdc5517" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667964} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea31cb84-3391-51fb-8fe2-69c560164572" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668259}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e22d897d-f7ce-5b4f-b6d4-aa4c45c66b5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-141096" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-2y.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=-2{e}^{-2x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4{e}^{-2x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2y \\\\ 4{e}^{-2x} & \\overset{?}{=}-2(-2{e}^{-2x}) \\\\ 4{e}^{-2x} & =4{e}^{-2x}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=-2{e}^{-2x}$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=-2{e}^{x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-2{e}^{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2y \\\\ -2{e}^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}-2(-2{e}^{x}) \\\\ -2{e}^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}4{e}^{x} \\\\ 0 & \\ne 6{e}^{x}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=-2{e}^{x}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=2{e}^{-x}+1,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-2{e}^{-x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2y \\\\ -2{e}^{-x} & \\overset{?}{=}-2(2{e}^{-x}+1) \\\\ -2{e}^{-x} & \\overset{?}{=}-4{e}^{-x}-2 \\\\ 2{e}^{-x} & \\ne -2.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=2{e}^{-x}+1$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $y=-2{e}^{-2x}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106054 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105861 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16a6f0f7-4003-5908-8b1b-68d218fdcb8f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Function Is a Valid PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28290577-9f35-5129-b322-2adb5a89d8eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459575} {:answer/id #uuid "2a7099ba-c89d-5357-8ac5-0eb5f8d4bfdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459576}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a7099ba-c89d-5357-8ac5-0eb5f8d4bfdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459576} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8c87803-66b8-5493-95c8-0fd1fdbe648f" :answer-field/key "$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460654} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba3373bb-57e2-52ac-96d5-c7830669ab8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459577} {:answer/id #uuid "fe8f41d5-faf8-5a40-8abc-89296cb486aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe8f41d5-faf8-5a40-8abc-89296cb486aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459578} :answer-field/id #uuid "c85e7583-1b83-519f-be37-87bd35fc0298" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460655} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f4039ed-a206-589f-a7f0-146b4b5ad449" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459579} {:answer/id #uuid "63e48fac-24b2-5157-8ea7-06915d7a1801" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459580}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63e48fac-24b2-5157-8ea7-06915d7a1801" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459580} :answer-field/id #uuid "391e78e0-03f7-5e20-b3ae-005291d57d59" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460656} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20abbc12-e051-547e-a664-1ab4366bdd37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667968} {:answer/id #uuid "0ea73f2b-feb5-5a01-b8e3-8d5132a1774a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667969}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20abbc12-e051-547e-a664-1ab4366bdd37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667968} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e48cf12-915f-5882-ab4d-7f5fc3ad0110" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668261}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "131f397c-26fd-57a9-a7d9-cabc7db579b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-158315" :question/problem "![](images/88/8835c085ca34d59f5c79786e12ed67cb33ccfdcfefd706dcc83ca2be0239670f.png)\n\nConsider the function $f(x)$ whose graph is shown above.\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2},\\, & 0<x<1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement “$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x$” is true. From the graph, we see that $f(x)$ is nonnegative for all $x.$\n\n- Statement ${\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$ is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[{1}^{3}]-[{0}^{3}] \\\\  & =1-0 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ is a valid probability density function” is true. Since statements “$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x$” and ${\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$ are true, $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x$”; ${\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$; “$f(x)$ is a valid probability density function”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106297 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105769 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "32467c2c-5605-50e9-b961-a29535a0effb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9fa458c3-7282-53ea-a5bc-e0d9c9649ae4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477265} {:answer/id #uuid "6323e003-b566-54fd-8ad4-a54a9bcf1cc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477266}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9fa458c3-7282-53ea-a5bc-e0d9c9649ae4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477265} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ff5f153-df81-5564-84ec-df4c0c2a6cb4" :answer-field/key "$v=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$ is an eigenvector of $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477602} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "927430a2-7643-57f4-820b-091a125a9885" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477267} {:answer/id #uuid "9bb94d42-b075-53e5-a318-c0b8c764abd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477268}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bb94d42-b075-53e5-a318-c0b8c764abd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477268} :answer-field/id #uuid "783247a3-0ebe-54a6-98ea-9862b85cfe12" :answer-field/key "$v=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ is an eigenvector of $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =0.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477603} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "514a35aa-74e7-586d-b428-f5e95b6fdef4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477269} {:answer/id #uuid "aec979f1-be2c-5a54-b2f4-f82b778d6eaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477270}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "514a35aa-74e7-586d-b428-f5e95b6fdef4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477269} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8624b7d-1161-5bdc-b93a-f2003b597423" :answer-field/key "If $v$ is an eigenvector of a matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2,$ then $3v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to $\\lambda =6.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477604} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9143d9f1-991a-53ca-9e01-44223f07a318" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668042} {:answer/id #uuid "ab7a6c49-4763-586d-aa95-dc7d2ee3b03c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668043}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9143d9f1-991a-53ca-9e01-44223f07a318" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668042} :answer-field/id #uuid "93ff967c-c2ef-5adb-888b-b54d3966ecb6" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668298}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2b717856-6a11-5857-bbda-def4fc991b4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-36792" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ With that in mind, let's examine the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement “$v=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$ is an eigenvector of $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2.$” is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =1v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSince $Av=v,$ we conclude that $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =1$ (but not $2$).\n\n- Statement “$v=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ is an eigenvector of $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =0.$” is true. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{v}_{1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =0\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =0{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSince $Av=0v,$ we conclude that $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =0.$\n\n- Statement “If $v$ is an eigenvector of a matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2,$ then $3v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to $\\lambda =6.$” is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A(3v)=3Av=3(2v)=2(3v).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince, $A(3v)=2(3v),$ and $3v\\ne 0,$ this implies that $3v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =2$ (but not $6$).\n\n**Note:** In general, any non-zero multiple of an eigenvector is again an eigenvector, and the corresponding eigenvalue is the same.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$v=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ is an eigenvector of $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =0.$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106298 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105769 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "32467c2c-5605-50e9-b961-a29535a0effb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fff2517f-6ee9-5857-849b-e8bac0566892" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459883} {:answer/id #uuid "5804ba63-871c-5ec3-9143-f1db8543491f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459884}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5804ba63-871c-5ec3-9143-f1db8543491f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459884} :answer-field/id #uuid "556c67f5-271f-5f49-84eb-27b172350fdc" :answer-field/key "$v=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ is an eigenvector of $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =1.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460808} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02048e2e-d9e1-557d-8b5d-99f7bdac06ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459885} {:answer/id #uuid "9ee4cd8c-6049-5a47-91b4-7b276dbb6b7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459886}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ee4cd8c-6049-5a47-91b4-7b276dbb6b7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459886} :answer-field/id #uuid "554a250b-6b90-5daf-85cd-bd88cf2dcbb0" :answer-field/key "If $v$ is an eigenvector of a matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-7$ then $3v$ is also an eigenvector corresponding to $\\lambda =-7.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460809} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "319ac9f3-074e-58d8-9580-d87719d9124d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459887} {:answer/id #uuid "ec56c825-4131-57f6-85e5-525e8c9cfb15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "319ac9f3-074e-58d8-9580-d87719d9124d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459887} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae7a14e2-54a4-5d30-9573-5c686b8bbc8c" :answer-field/key "$v=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ is an eigenvector of $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $0.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460810} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1daab29e-6138-5668-8be3-4f0c4ae5eb4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668046} {:answer/id #uuid "8a58e44c-34c9-50dc-b7d1-8042fa1cb409" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1daab29e-6138-5668-8be3-4f0c4ae5eb4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668046} :answer-field/id #uuid "55fda70d-eb88-5da5-80c6-1700c1f45878" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668300}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c27f53bd-6979-5472-9b95-f9c6b5cc1260" :question/math-academy-id "q-37087" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ With that in mind, let's examine the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement “$v=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ is an eigenvector of $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =1.$” is true. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =1v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “If $v$ is an eigenvector of a matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-7$ then $3v$ is also an eigenvector corresponding to $\\lambda =-7.$” is true. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A(3v)=3Av=3(-7v)=-7(3v).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince, $A(3v)=-7(3v),$ and $3v\\ne 0,$ this implies that $3v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =-7.$\n\n**Note:** In general, any non-zero multiple of an eigenvector is again an eigenvector, and the corresponding eigenvalue is the same.\n\n- Statement “$v=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ is an eigenvector of $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $0.$” is false. An eigenvector must be a *non-zero* vector.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$v=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ is an eigenvector of $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =1.$”; “If $v$ is an eigenvector of a matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-7$ then $3v$ is also an eigenvector corresponding to $\\lambda =-7.$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111171 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110587 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b834b64-9679-56c2-b5e9-ee26a54b5e13" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Values in the Domain of the Inverse Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e068923-3d10-550d-8421-14bddad9a0e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477313} {:answer/id #uuid "7317a4d6-2129-5d1e-8fab-a3b1303db8a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477314}] :answer-field/correct