V](images/46/4651b8b75b33ee763d138713d25e4255b607851f1fd53cdbbf2de2e89a82f590.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440186} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b3de0a6-37a3-5b94-8013-f31dfce8ca2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668044} {:answer/id #uuid "74e3b1ea-b0f7-5603-af7d-f1a95f56e851" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668045}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b3de0a6-37a3-5b94-8013-f31dfce8ca2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668044} :answer-field/id #uuid "aee2bd93-469d-58a6-aeb3-6798efecf00b" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668299}] :question/id #uuid "4763915f-8f50-5b34-9b27-a90ea817e8a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-36897" :question/problem "Which of the graphs below correspond to an invertible function?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Graph I is strictly increasing. Graph II has a local minimum and maximum, graph III first decreases to a visible local minimum and then increases, and graph IV is a downward parabola. Thus II, III, and IV fail the horizontal line test; only I is invertible."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125081 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124654 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ca319c5-9f62-51e3-b670-611fc8a8daaa" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a Critical Point Using the Second Partial Derivatives Test"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bec17f64-ce69-5230-bea1-4c2615d74f42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459903} {:answer/id #uuid "85c18489-dea6-5fb2-9d89-130fc5c1b1f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459904}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bec17f64-ce69-5230-bea1-4c2615d74f42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459903} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd2a276f-7803-5f65-bd33-68a28b7e31e7" :answer-field/key "$H(0,0)>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460818} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40e11471-46d4-5799-baa9-0365abcd187d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459905} {:answer/id #uuid "8c89fe41-d355-532f-86db-ab83615e7527" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459906}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40e11471-46d4-5799-baa9-0365abcd187d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459905} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef36775a-81e3-5b08-b904-d9c79629c51f" :answer-field/key "$\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(0,0)<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460819} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "006f50e8-ea05-5741-a308-013abd32cd8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459907} {:answer/id #uuid "7065b35a-f55c-5614-bf1d-f97f8189b949" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459908}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7065b35a-f55c-5614-bf1d-f97f8189b949" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459908} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cf97acc-e472-5185-819a-c5d932fd7c68" :answer-field/key "The point $(0,0)$ is a saddle point of $f$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460820} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d603974-5387-5069-8eab-ab22a9bc6977" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668050} {:answer/id #uuid "f492c370-2fc4-59a9-b998-5afff32251ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668051}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d603974-5387-5069-8eab-ab22a9bc6977" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668050} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7b36f5d-0546-57e9-a8df-ff616edb6aa0" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668302}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c3ea19ab-9bf6-5660-afe0-39f6942a18e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-37588" :question/problem "The function \n$f(x,y)$\nhas the first derivative\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}2x & -2y\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nand has a stationary point at $(0,0).$ If $H$ denotes the Hessian determinant of $f,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The second partial derivative test states that if $a\\in {R}^{2}$ is a stationary point of $f(x,y)$ with Hessian determinant $H(a),$ we have the following:\n\n- If $H(a)>0,$ then:\n\n- if $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(a)<0,$ then $f$ has a local maximum at $a$\n\n- if $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(a)>0,$ then $f$ has a local minimum at $a$\n\n- If $H(a)<0,$ then $f$ has a saddle point at $a$\n\n- If $H(a)=0,$ then the second partial derivatives test is inconclusive.\n\nFirst, we notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}2x,\\,-2y\\end{bmatrix},$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-2y.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x)=2 \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-2y)=-2 \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-2y)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(0,0),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(0,0)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement $H(0,0)>0$ is false. Computing the determinant of ${f}^{″}(0,0),$ we get\n\n$$\nH(0,0)=det({f}^{″}(0,0))=2\\cdot (-2)-{0}^{2}=-4<0.\n$$\n\n- Statement $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(0,0)<0$ is false. We have $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(0,0)=({f}^{″}(0,0))_{11}=2.$\n\n- Statement “The point $(0,0)$ is a saddle point of $f$” is true. Indeed, since $H(0,0)<0,$ the point $(0,0)$ is a saddle point by the second partial derivative test.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The point $(0,0)$ is a saddle point of $f$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125118 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124521 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9d77214-796e-558f-a364-00ae3e25cc13" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "341579a5-829a-5c6f-b9ae-ac1104715fc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answe